% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 38% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 4. Contract [1], for 14,734.08 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar patterns can occur due to seasonal demand or budget cycles. Small amounts near the limit do not prove violations, as prices may naturally approach the threshold.\nWhat can be checked: Check if multiple contracts in December cover the same need. Review awardee A’s contracts to see if they repeat the same services. Contract [1] shows a near-threshold amount; compare it with other December contracts to identify patterns.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["%2FxPHjhmcHMK5HQrHoP3G5A%3D%3D","QmAh%2F4q459x%2FR5QFTlaM4A%3D%3D","bKVggo0GW2msNfRW6APEDw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}